

Mapping of different formats to the core Yarfraw models

	Yarfraw provides a unified data model for all the feed formats that it supports. 
Yarfraw's core data model is based from Rss 2.0, feed elements in other formats are mapped to these Rss 2.0 fields.
The following table shows the mapping between feed elements in different format to Yarfraw's data model. If an element is not mapped,
it will still be available in the *.otherElements list. Unmapped attributes are in *.otherAttributes map.

	This means you can easily write a conversion utility to convert between different feed format, simply reads the original format,
write it to a file using a different format setting. For example, to convert a Rss 2.0 feed to Rss 1.0:

+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+

    FeedReader r = new FeedReader("rss20.xml");
    Channel c = r.readChannel();
    
    File f = File.createTempFile("rss10", ".xml");
    FeedWriter w = new FeedWriter(f);
    w.setFormat(FeedFormat.RSS10);
    w.writeChannel(c);
    
    //of course, you can read the converted feed
    r.setFormat(FeedFormat.RSS10);
    r.setFile(f);
    Channel c2 = r.readChannel();
  
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+


Reading a RSS 2.0 feed

	You can use the reader class to read any RSS 2.0 feed.
	
	
	
		
	Similar to FeedWriter, you can add your own event handler:
	
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
   
  r.readChannel(new ValidationEventHandler(){
      public boolean handleEvent(ValidationEvent event) {
      	//Process the event
        return false;
      }
  });
   
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
